On Monday, November 16, 2015 at 2:41:06 AM UTC+3, John Cowan wrote:
>
> Robin Lee Powell scripsit: 
>
> > It turns out they can't put any writing anywhere except the spine, 
> > and that's the only ink color.  If we're going with cloth bound, our 
> > choice is what you see in those pictures, or the same thing but with 
> > blue binding instead of grey.  That's our *only* choice. 
>
> Bogus, but if that's what we've got, then that's what we've got. 
> I definitely prefer gray to blue. 
>
> Is this still the text of the First Edition, or with the errors on the 
> errata page corrected?  (I assume it can't possibly be the Second Edition 
> (dotside, xorlo, etc.) yet.)


In the branch Robin is talking about only minor things have been fixed.

Dotside, xorlo and other new things are being fixed but not in what Robin 
is talking about.
The new edition is being done here: 
https://github.com/lojban/cll/tree/docbook-prince-cll-2.0
When a certain level is fixed it will be forked into CLL 1.5 branch which 
will get only stability fixes while branch 2.0 will continue its 
development.

 

>  If the latter, don't forget to update the 
> license inside the book to CC-BY, or whatever we are using. 
>
> > If we want a dust jacket, someone (presumably Matt Arnold) has to go 
> > make it.  I suppose we could give someone money to do so. 
>
> I'm in favor of that, given the lack of writing on the front cover. 
> If we could make the jacket at least partly red, so much the better, 
> so that the name "Red Book" wouldn't seem completely irrational. 
>
> Otherwise LGTM. 
